---
id: org.dxos.plugin.claude
name: ClaudePlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

Models Anthropic Claude managed agents — agents Anthropic hosts and runs on your
behalf — as objects in the space. A `ClaudeManagedAgent` holds the configuration
(model, system prompt, toolsets, skills, MCP servers) and, once deployed, the
server-assigned agent id. A `ClaudeAgentSession` records one run of that agent.

Configuration and execution are deliberately separate: the object is edited
locally and pushed to Anthropic by an explicit deploy step, so a half-configured
agent never reaches the API. Session events are not mirrored into the space; the
transcript is fetched on demand from the session id.

The plugin also offers Claude Code on this computer as an agent a project's
tasks can be assigned to. An `AgentHelper` host runs it through the Claude Code
ACP adapter this plugin ships, against the user's own `claude`, and the chat
holds its session. The plugin owns that host's interface and the agent server
behind it; its Tauri-only module runs the server as the desktop app's `dx-agent`
sidecar, and plugin-dev-shell runs the same server inside a Vite dev server.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term   | URI                            |
|--------|--------------------------------|
| `type` | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`        |
| `feat` | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`        |
| `scenario` | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0`    |
| `test` | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`        |
| `decision` | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0` |

## Types

```mdl
type ClaudeManagedAgent
  desc: |
    The configuration of a Claude managed agent. The Anthropic `agent_…` id is a
    foreign key in object meta (source "anthropic.com"), not a field; it and
    `agentVersion` are absent until the agent has been deployed at least once.
  fields:
    name: string
    description?: string
    model: string                # Anthropic model id; defaults to claude-opus-5
    effort?: string              # low | medium | high | xhigh | max
    systemPrompt?: string
    tools?: string[]             # toolset type ids, default [agent_toolset_20260401]
    skills?: string[]            # Anthropic skill ids, e.g. xlsx
    mcpServers?: { name, url }[]
    environmentId?: string       # env_… sessions run in
    agentVersion?: number
    status: string               # draft | deployed | archived
```

```mdl
type ClaudeAgentSession
  desc: |
    One run of a ClaudeManagedAgent, hosted by Anthropic. The Anthropic `sess_…`
    id is a foreign key in object meta (source "anthropic.com"), not a field.
  fields:
    title: string
    agent: Ref<ClaudeManagedAgent>
    environmentId: string
    vaultId?: string             # vlt_… holding the credentials bound to the run
    status?: string              # last observed API status
    stopReason?: string          # why the agent last went idle
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Schema

  req F-1.1:
    when: plugin is activated
    then: ClaudeManagedAgent and ClaudeAgentSession are registered with the schema module
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Agent Configuration

  req F-2.1:
    when: Create Claude Agent is invoked with a name
    then: |
      a ClaudeManagedAgent is added to the space with model defaulting to
      claude-opus-5, tools defaulting to [agent_toolset_20260401] and status
      "draft", and the operation returns its object id. No request is made to
      Anthropic.

  req F-2.2:
    when: List Claude Agents is invoked
    then: every ClaudeManagedAgent in the space is returned with its id, name,
          model, status, agentId and environmentId
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Deployment

  req F-3.1:
    when: Deploy Claude Agent is invoked for an agent with no Anthropic key
    then: |
      POST /v1/agents is called with the projected configuration, the returned
      id is written as a foreign key under source "anthropic.com", and the
      version is stored with status "deployed"

  req F-3.2:
    when: Deploy Claude Agent is invoked for an agent that already has a key
    then: |
      POST /v1/agents/{agentId} is called with the stored agentVersion for
      optimistic concurrency, the key is replaced rather than appended, and the
      new version is stored

  req F-3.3:
    when: the projected configuration has no tools, skills or MCP servers
    then: those keys are omitted from the request body rather than sent empty
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Sessions

  req F-4.1:
    when: Start Claude Agent Session is invoked for an agent that has not been deployed
    then: the operation fails with AgentNotDeployedError and no session is created

  req F-4.2:
    when: Start Claude Agent Session is invoked with no environment id on the
          agent and none in the input
    then: |
      a default cloud environment is created via POST /v1/environments, its id
      is stored on the agent so later runs reuse it, and the operation returns
      provisionedEnvironment: true

  req F-4.3:
    when: Start Claude Agent Session is invoked with a message
    then: |
      POST /v1/sessions is called with the agent id, environment id and the
      message as a single `user.message` initial event, and a ClaudeAgentSession
      is added to the space keyed by the returned session id

  req F-4.4:
    when: Start Claude Agent Session is invoked
    then: |
      a vault is created for the run and passed as the session's only `vault_ids`
      entry — always, credentials or not, since `vault_ids` is fixed at session
      creation — and its id is stored on the ClaudeAgentSession

  req F-4.5:
    when: Send Message To Claude Agent is invoked
    then: a `user.message` event is posted to the session; the operation does not
          wait for the agent to reply

  req F-4.6:
    when: Get Claude Agent Transcript is invoked
    then: |
      the session state and its events are read, the object's status and
      stopReason are refreshed, and the user/agent text turns are returned

  req F-4.7:
    when: Get Claude Agent Transcript is invoked without an `order`
    then: |
      the LAST `limit` events are read (order=desc) and returned chronologically;
      order: first reads the opening events instead
```

```mdl
feat F-5: Skill

  req F-5.1:
    when: plugin is activated
    then: the org.dxos.skill.claude skill is contributed with all eight
          operations as tools

  req F-5.2:
    note: |
      The skill instructions state the create → deploy → run ordering, since a
      session runs the deployed copy and silently ignores unpushed edits.
```

```mdl
feat F-6: Credentials

  req F-6.1:
    when: any operation calls the Anthropic API
    then: the API key is resolved from the credential stored under the
          "anthropic.com" service and sent as the `x-api-key` header

  req F-6.3:
    when: no "anthropic.com" credential exists in the space
    then: |
      the operation fails with MissingCredentialError (a typed failure, not a
      defect), and the skill instructs the model to enable the connectors skill
      and render the integration prompt for anthropic.com rather than stopping

  req F-6.2:
    when: the API returns a non-2xx response
    then: the operation fails with ClaudeAgentApiError carrying the status and body

  req F-6.4:
    when: a GET fails on transport, 429 or 5xx
    then: |
      it is retried up to three times with a fixed one-second delay; a 4xx other
      than 429 fails immediately, since the request itself is what was rejected

  req F-6.5:
    when: a POST fails on transport or 5xx
    then: |
      it is NOT retried — a lost response is indistinguishable from one never
      sent, and a retry would create the session, vault or credential twice; only
      429, where the server says it did not act, is retried
```

```mdl
feat F-7: Session credentials

  req F-7.1:
    when: Start Claude Agent Session is invoked with `credentials`
    then: |
      each referenced AccessToken is resolved through the credentials service and
      stored in the session's vault as an `environment_variable` credential named
      by `as`, with unrestricted networking (host-scoped substitution 401s sibling
      hosts, e.g. api.github.com under a github.com scope); the operation returns
      the names bound and never a value

  req F-7.2:
    when: Set Claude Agent Session Credentials is invoked with a name already bound
    then: |
      the stored credential's secret is rotated in place rather than added a
      second time (names are unique within a vault), and the change takes effect
      on the running session's next operation without restarting it

  req F-7.5:
    when: the credentials list repeats an environment variable name, or the vault
          holds more credentials than one listing page
    then: |
      the repeated name keeps its last entry and the listing is followed to its
      last page — both cases would otherwise create a name that already exists
      and be rejected as a conflict

  req F-7.6:
    when: a referenced token resolves to an empty value
    then: the operation fails with CredentialResolutionError naming the variable,
          rather than binding a blank secret the agent only discovers as a 401

  req F-7.3:
    when: Set or Revoke Claude Agent Session Credentials is invoked for a session
          with no vault id
    then: the operation fails with SessionVaultMissingError, since `vault_ids`
          cannot be added to an existing session

  req F-7.4:
    when: Revoke Claude Agent Session Credentials is invoked
    then: |
      each named credential is archived, purging the secret and freeing the name;
      a name that is not bound fails with CredentialNotBoundError rather than
      reporting a revocation that did not happen
```

```mdl
feat F-8: Claude Code on this computer

  req F-8.1:
    when: the plugin is enabled in the desktop app and `claude` is installed
    then: Claude Code is a registered agent, and a task's menu offers "Assign to Claude Code"

  req F-8.2:
    when: the plugin is enabled outside the desktop app, or `claude` is not found
    then: the menu entry is shown disabled with the reason

  req F-8.3:
    when: a task is assigned to Claude Code
    then: |
      Claude Code works in a git worktree of the project's code folder on this
      device, its session streams into the chat, and a tool call it asks
      permission for waits on a card in the chat until someone answers it

  req F-8.4:
    when: Claude Code runs a session
    then: |
      Composer's operations are offered as the `composer` MCP server, scoped to
      the chat's space; its read-only tools run without asking

  req F-8.5:
    when: Claude Code runs a turn in a chat with MCP connections switched on
    then: |
      each connection's MCP server is offered to the session, a connection's
      credential never appearing in Claude Code's configuration; switching
      one on or off reloads the session from the next turn
```

```mdl
feat F-9: Claude Code (cloud)

  req F-9.1:
    when: the plugin is enabled
    then: |
      Claude Code is offered on EDGE in a chat's agent picker and as
      "Assign to Claude Code (EDGE)" in a task's menu, and runs Claude Code in
      an EDGE sandbox rather than on this computer

  req F-9.2:
    when: a turn runs on Claude Code (cloud)
    then: |
      the agent runs with the space's Claude subscription OAuth token as
      `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`, never with an Anthropic API key, and with its
      GitHub token as `GITHUB_TOKEN`/`GH_TOKEN`, so `git` and `gh` can clone,
      push and open pull requests; a space holding only an API key lends no
      Claude credential and logs a warning

  req F-9.3:
    when: the chat belongs to a project with repositories
    then: |
      the sandbox checks them out before the agent's first turn, and the agent
      works in the first one, with the others as additional directories, so it
      reads the CLAUDE.md, skills and settings of every one of them

  req F-9.4:
    when: a chat is switched to Claude Code (cloud) before its first message
    then: that first message runs on Claude Code (cloud), not on the default assistant

  req F-9.5:
    when: a chat runs on Claude Code, on this computer or on EDGE, before its first message
    then: |
      the agent picker offers the chat's model (Opus, Sonnet, Haiku), effort
      (Low to Max) and permissions (Ask before acting, Accept edits, Auto,
      Bypass permissions), each defaulting to Claude Code's default and the
      plugin's permission setting; the choices are fixed once the chat has
      started, and EDGE reports the mode and model the agent actually runs with
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: Config projection defaults and omissions
  given: a ClaudeManagedAgent with only a name
  when: toAgentConfig is applied
  then:
    - model === "claude-opus-5"
    - tools === [{ type: "agent_toolset_20260401" }]
    - the body has no `skills` or `mcp_servers` key
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: Effort is projected onto the model object
  given: a ClaudeManagedAgent with effort "high"
  when: toAgentConfig is applied
  then: model === { id: "claude-opus-5", effort: "high" }
```

```mdl
scenario T-3: Transcript keeps prose only
  given: an event list mixing user.message, agent.message, agent.tool_use and
         session.status_idle events
  when: toTranscript is applied
  then:
    - only the user and agent messages remain, in order
    - an agent.message with no text block is dropped
```

```mdl
scenario T-4: Method-specific retryable statuses
  given: GET and POST requests with ClaudeAgentApiError values
  when: isRetryable is applied
  then:
    - a GET retries 0, 429 and 503
    - a POST retries only 429
    - neither retries 400, 401 or 404
```

## QA

Executable tests. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by test and step number.

```mdl
test QA-1: Configure, deploy and run a Claude managed agent
  desc: |
    The full round-trip — create a local agent configuration, deploy it to Anthropic, start a
    session and read the transcript back. Deploy and everything after it calls the live
    Anthropic API and needs an "anthropic.com" credential in the space; a QA environment cannot
    assume one exists, so those steps are blocked rather than run.
  actors: both
  covers: [F-1.1, F-2.1, F-2.2, F-3.1, F-4.1, F-4.3, F-4.4, F-4.6]
  status: blocked
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - collection: a collection in that space, to create into
    - plugin-claude is enabled — it is OFF by default, and no claude operation is
      registered until it is on. Enabling is a UI action (Settings -> plugin registry);
      `manager.enable()` returns without error from the debug port and does not enable it.
    - no ClaudeManagedAgent named "QA Agent" exists — ABORT rather than deleting one this test
      did not create
  steps:
    - name: Create the agent configuration
      do: In the navtree, click + on a collection and choose Claude Agent. Name it "QA Agent".
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.claude.createAgent { name: "QA Agent" }
      capture: created
      expect: a ClaudeManagedAgent named "QA Agent" exists, status "draft", model defaulting to
        claude-opus-5, and no request was made to Anthropic
      assert: return !!$created.id;
    - name: List agents
      do: Open the agent's list view (or ask the assistant to list Claude agents).
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.claude.listAgents {}
      expect: "QA Agent" appears in the returned list with status "draft"
      assert: return $result.agents.some((a) => a.id === $created.id);
    - name: Deploy the agent
      do: Click "Deploy" on "QA Agent".
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.claude.deployAgent { agent: $created.id }
      expect: the agent's status becomes "deployed" and it carries an Anthropic `agent_…` foreign
        key
      blocked: |
        Calls the live Anthropic API (POST /v1/agents) and requires an "anthropic.com" credential
        resolved through the credentials service (F-6.1); no such credential can be assumed to
        exist in a QA space, and deploying for real would create a billable agent on Anthropic's
        servers as a side effect of running this spec. Requires a dedicated QA credential and
        environment before this step (and everything downstream of it) can run.
    - name: Start a session
      do: Click "Run" on the deployed "QA Agent" and enter a first message.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.claude.startSession { agent: $created.id, message: "Say hello." }
      capture: session
      expect: a ClaudeAgentSession is added to the space, keyed by the Anthropic session id, with
        its own vault
      blocked: Depends on the deployed agent from the previous (blocked) step.
    - name: Read the transcript
      do: Open the session and watch its transcript.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.claude.getTranscript { session: $session.id }
      expect: the user's message and the agent's reply appear, in order, and the session status
        refreshes
      blocked: Depends on the running session from the previous (blocked) step.
  after:
    - name: Delete the agent
      do: Right-click "QA Agent" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [$created.id], target: $given.collection }
      expect: the row leaves the navtree
```

```mdl
test QA-2: Assign a project task to Claude Code
  desc: |
    A project task goes to Claude Code on this computer, which works in its own
    git worktree, marks the task through Composer's tools, and continues the
    same session in a follow-up. Coding agents keep their default permission
    mode, auto, so Claude asks only before a risky action. Walked by the autocue
    flow `packages/plugins/plugin-claude/autocue/claude-code-task.mjs`.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-8.1, F-8.3, F-8.4]
  status: verified
  given:
    - Composer is the desktop app (for autocue, the test build from
      `moon run composer-app:tauri-build-test`)
    - `claude` is installed and signed in on this computer
    - a git repository on this computer for the project (the flow seeds one)
    - space: a space is open
  steps:
    - name: Enable the Claude plugin
      do: Open Plugins, filter for "Claude" and switch it on.
      expect: Claude is enabled, and the Code plugin with it
    - name: Create a project
      do: Click + on the space, choose Project, name it "Greeter" and save.
      expect: the project opens on its Overview, which has a "Code folder on this device" section
    - name: Choose the project's code folder
      do: Click "Choose folder…" and pick the repository.
      expect: the folder's path replaces "Not set"
    - name: Add a task
      do: |
        Open Tasks and add "Add a --shout flag to greet.js", described as "With
        --shout, print the greeting in capitals. Document the flag in the README."
      expect: the task is listed
    - name: Assign the task to Claude Code
      do: Open the task's menu and choose "Assign to Claude Code".
      expect: the task is started, and the project's chat holds the task brief as a context panel
    - name: Watch Claude work, allowing what it asks to run
      do: Open the Assistant companion and answer any permission card with Yes.
      expect: |
        commands, edits and Composer tool calls stream in, the turn ends with a
        summary, and the task is in review or done
    - name: Ask for more in a follow-up
      do: Send "Also accept -s as a short form of --shout, then commit." and allow what it asks to run.
      expect: |
        the same session continues and commits on a `composer/` branch of the
        repository, where `node greet.js Ada -s` prints HELLO, ADA!; `main` is unchanged
```

```mdl
test QA-3: Claude Code asks before every edit and command
  desc: |
    QA-2 with coding agents set to the `default` permission mode: each file
    edit and command Claude Code makes waits on a card in the chat. Walked by
    the same autocue flow with `AUTOCUE_AGENT_PERMISSIONS=default`.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-8.3]
  status: verified
  given:
    - as QA-2
  steps:
    - name: Enable the Claude plugin
      do: As QA-2.
      expect: Claude is enabled, and the Code plugin with it
    - name: Set coding agents to default permissions
      do: Open the Code plugin's settings and set "Coding agent permissions" to default.
      expect: the setting reads default
    - name: Assign a task as in QA-2
      do: Walk QA-2 from "Create a project" through "Assign the task to Claude Code".
      expect: the task is started
    - name: Watch Claude work, allowing each request
      do: Open the Assistant companion and answer each permission card with Yes.
      expect: |
        a card appears before each edit and command, Claude continues only once
        it is answered, and the task ends in review or done
    - name: Ask for more in a follow-up
      do: As QA-2, answering each card with Yes.
      expect: as QA-2, with a card before the commit
```

```mdl
test QA-4: A standalone chat on Claude Code (cloud) opens a pull request
  desc: |
    A chat switched to Claude Code (cloud) clones dxos/dxos in its EDGE sandbox
    with the space's GitHub token, opens a draft pull request, and closes it
    when asked. Walked by the autocue flow
    `packages/plugins/plugin-claude/autocue/claude-code-cloud-pr.mjs`.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-9.1, F-9.2, F-9.4]
  status: unverified        # 2026-10-21, the chat's options became the agent picker; re-run its flow
  given:
    - Composer against an EDGE that runs the coding agent
    - space: holds a Claude subscription token and a GitHub token that can push to dxos/dxos
  steps:
    - name: Create a chat
      do: Click + on the space and choose Chat.
      expect: an empty chat opens
    - name: Run the chat on Claude Code (cloud)
      do: Open the prompt's agent picker and choose Claude Code, then open it again and choose EDGE.
      expect: the picker reads Claude Code with the EDGE (cloud) icon
    - name: Ask it to clone dxos/dxos and open a pull request
      do: |
        Ask it to clone dxos/dxos, commit a one-line file on a new branch, push
        it and open a draft pull request with `gh pr create --draft`.
      expect: |
        the first reply comes from Claude Code, not the default assistant, and
        ends with the URL of an open draft pull request on dxos/dxos
    - name: Show the pull request on GitHub
      do: Open the pull request's URL.
      expect: the draft pull request with the one-line file
    - name: Ask it to close the pull request
      do: Ask it to close the pull request with `gh pr close --delete-branch`.
      expect: the pull request is closed and its branch deleted
```

```mdl
test QA-5: A project task on Claude Code (cloud) opens a pull request
  desc: |
    A project names dxos/dxos as its repository; a task assigned to Claude Code
    (cloud) is worked in an EDGE sandbox that checked the repository out, and
    the agent opens the draft pull request the task asks for. Walked by the
    autocue flow `packages/plugins/plugin-claude/autocue/claude-code-cloud-task.mjs`.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-9.1, F-9.2, F-9.3]
  status: unverified        # 2026-10-21, the task menu now reads "Assign to Claude Code (EDGE)"; re-run its flow
  given:
    - as QA-4
  steps:
    - name: Create a project
      do: Click + on the space, choose Project, name it "DXOS" and save.
      expect: the project opens
    - name: Give the project the dxos/dxos repository
      do: Add dxos/dxos to the project's repositories.
      expect: the project lists dxos/dxos
    - name: Add a task
      do: |
        Open Tasks and add a task asking for a short file on a new branch,
        pushed, with a draft pull request opened by `gh pr create --draft`.
      expect: the task is listed
    - name: Assign the task to Claude Code (cloud)
      do: Open the task's menu and choose "Assign to Claude Code (EDGE)".
      expect: the task is started and the project's chat opens on Claude Code (cloud)
    - name: Watch it open the pull request
      do: Open the Assistant companion.
      expect: the turn ends with the URL of an open draft pull request on dxos/dxos
    - name: Ask it to close the pull request
      do: Ask it in the same chat to close the pull request with `gh pr close --delete-branch`.
      expect: the pull request is closed and its branch deleted
```

```mdl
test QA-6: A chat chooses the model, effort and permissions of Claude Code
  desc: |
    The agent picker of a chat on Claude Code offers the model, effort and
    permissions the chat's session runs with. Walked by the autocue flow
    `packages/plugins/plugin-claude/autocue/claude-code-choices.mjs`.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-9.5]
  status: passing           # 2026-10-26, its autocue flow against a composer-app bundle on EDGE dev
  given:
    - Composer with the Claude plugin enabled
  steps:
    - name: Create a chat
      do: Click + on the space and choose Chat.
      expect: an empty chat opens
    - name: Run the chat on Claude Code
      do: Open the prompt's agent picker and choose Claude Code.
      expect: the picker reads Claude Code and offers Model, Effort and Permissions, each on Default
    - name: Choose Opus
      do: Open the agent picker and choose Opus under Model.
      expect: the picker reads Claude Code · Opus
    - name: Choose High effort
      do: Open the agent picker and choose High under Effort.
      expect: High is checked under Effort
    - name: Choose Bypass permissions
      do: Open the agent picker and choose Bypass permissions under Permissions.
      expect: Bypass permissions is checked under Permissions
```

